            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0107" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-18T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Your no. 147, April 17, 6 p.m. The President will speak at a meeting of the
                    Associated Press in New York on April 22, and will then deal appropriately with
                    the subject to which you refer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
